    "detailed_description": "<strong>God doesn't play dice games.<br>Because he likes slot machines.</strong><br><br><strong>4X4 PROGRESS</strong> is a new type of strategic design game.<br>You have to calculate the optimal layout to get a lot of resources and use them to advance your civilization,<br>but the layout you worked hard to make is randomly <strong>shuffled</strong> the next turn.<br>You can save only part of your layout by spending resources, but it's entirely up to the player how to save your layout efficiently.<br><br>The player becomes the god of one of 12 different civilizations and guides them from the Stone Age to the modern era.<br>In a small <strong>4X4 panel</strong>, you place various tiles such as cities, farmlands, and mines, and depending on the layout, you have to get resources and induce technological development to advance your civilization.<br>Of course, each civilization has its own unique tiles, so you can enjoy different gameplay for each civilization.<br><br>Defend your civilization from the attacks of enemies that invade at regular intervals,<br>and can your civilization launch a rocket into space?<br><br>You can play as the following civilizations!<br>1. Russia<br>2. Japan<br>3. Egypt<br>4. Arabia<br>5. Germany<br>6. America<br>7. Maori<br>8. Inca<br>9. England<br>10. Korea<br>11. Zulu<br>12. China<br>..You can also enjoy various other civilizations as DLCs!<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>A new strategic design game where you have to calculate the optimal layout but control the randomness.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Choose your favorite civilization among 12 civilizations and enjoy an alternate history simulation from the Stone Age to the modern era in different ways for each civilization.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Various difficulty settings that induce a sense of challenge</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>70+ historical tiles with 8-bit graphics.</li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<strong>God doesn't play dice games.<br>Because he likes slot machines.</strong><br><br><strong>4X4 PROGRESS</strong> is a new type of strategic design game.<br>You have to calculate the optimal layout to get a lot of resources and use them to advance your civilization,<br>but the layout you worked hard to make is randomly <strong>shuffled</strong> the next turn.<br>You can save only part of your layout by spending resources, but it's entirely up to the player how to save your layout efficiently.<br><br>The player becomes the god of one of 12 different civilizations and guides them from the Stone Age to the modern era.<br>In a small <strong>4X4 panel</strong>, you place various tiles such as cities, farmlands, and mines, and depending on the layout, you have to get resources and induce technological development to advance your civilization.<br>Of course, each civilization has its own unique tiles, so you can enjoy different gameplay for each civilization.<br><br>Defend your civilization from the attacks of enemies that invade at regular intervals,<br>and can your civilization launch a rocket into space?<br><br>You can play as the following civilizations!<br>1. Russia<br>2. Japan<br>3. Egypt<br>4. Arabia<br>5. Germany<br>6. America<br>7. Maori<br>8. Inca<br>9. England<br>10. Korea<br>11. Zulu<br>12. China<br>..You can also enjoy various other civilizations as DLCs!<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>A new strategic design game where you have to calculate the optimal layout but control the randomness.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Choose your favorite civilization among 12 civilizations and enjoy an alternate history simulation from the Stone Age to the modern era in different ways for each civilization.</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Various difficulty settings that induce a sense of challenge</li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>70+ historical tiles with 8-bit graphics.</li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Choose your desired civilization, design your 4x4 cities with the most efficient layout, and advance your civilization! However, the layout is reset every turn.",
